  "question": {
    "text": "When the wavelength of radiation falling on a metal is changed from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mi>nm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>200</mn><mi>nm</mi></math>, the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons becomes three times larger. The work function of the metal is close to:"
